---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Research" description="Research program — Diagnose → Build → Adapt. How people mis-rely on AI outputs, whether interventions can improve appropriate reliance, and whether AI can adapt to individual trust context.">
  <div class="container-content py-14">
    <div class="max-w-[820px]">

      <!-- 1. Page introduction -->
      <span class="section-kicker mb-3">Research program</span>
      <h1 class="mb-4">Diagnose → Build → Adapt</h1>
      <p class="lead mb-3">
        How people mis-rely on AI outputs; whether interventions and systems can improve appropriate reliance; and whether AI can respond to individual trust context.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-12 max-w-2xl">
        This is the recurring question set behind <em>human–AI decision-making under uncertainty</em>. Each stage below is a line of work with its own evidence class — historical measurement, active intervention, and simulation — rather than a set of parallel contributions.
      </p>

      <!-- 2. Research arc — three editorial sections -->
      <section id="diagnose" class="mb-12">
        <div class="arc-item" style="border-top-width:0; padding-top:0">
          <span class="arc-index">01 · Diagnose</span>
          <h2 class="arc-question mt-2 mb-3">How and why do people mis-rely on AI outputs?</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-5">
            This stage asks what miscalibration looks like: how unsupported numerical precision and weak evidential support shape trust and reliance. The Precision-Illusion taxonomy and FitCalib-Bench record the measurement and audit work behind this question. They are historical assets — they inform the question without pretending to be active research.
          </p>
          <div class="related-list">
            <div class="related-item">
              <span class="rel-role">Measurement · historical</span>
              <a href="/blog/precision-illusion-intro/" class="link-arrow">Precision Illusion taxonomy →</a>
            </div>
            <div class="related-item">
              <span class="rel-role">Audit · closed</span>
              <a href="/research/measuring-ai-reliability/fitcalib-bench/" class="link-arrow">FitCalib-Bench controlled audit →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="build" class="mb-12">
        <div class="arc-item">
          <span class="arc-index">02 · Build</span>
          <h2 class="arc-question mt-2 mb-3">Can systems improve appropriate reliance?</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-5">
            The most active stage. CheckMyCoach tests whether evidential-limit failures in AI advice can be operationally detected, routed, and repaired without overstating certainty. InteractionKit is the typed measurement infrastructure the agenda builds on. CheckMyCoach human validation is the current empirical step — no human-participant findings are claimed.
          </p>
          <div class="related-list">
            <div class="related-item">
              <span class="rel-role">Intervention · active</span>
              <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/checkmycoach/" class="link-arrow">CheckMyCoach →</a>
            </div>
            <div class="related-item">
              <span class="rel-role">Infrastructure · released</span>
              <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/interactionkit/" class="link-arrow">InteractionKit v1.0.0 →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="adapt" class="mb-12">
        <div class="arc-item">
          <span class="arc-index">03 · Adapt</span>
          <h2 class="arc-question mt-2 mb-3">Can AI respond to individual trust context?</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-5">
            When a static intervention is insufficient, the agenda asks whether the system can adapt to the person in front of it. CalTrust is a simulation-only prototype exploring this question — reported proxy metrics describe the simulator, not human trust.
          </p>
          <div class="related-list">
            <div class="related-item">
              <span class="rel-role">Simulation · prototype</span>
              <a href="/research/understanding-human-trust/caltrust/" class="link-arrow">CalTrust →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. Cross-program synthesis -->
      <section id="synthesis" class="mb-12">
        <span class="section-kicker mb-2">Synthesis</span>
        <h2 class="mt-1 mb-3">Why these three stages belong together</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          Miscalibration is first <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium">diagnosed</strong> as an evidential mismatch between what an AI system knows and what it communicates. Interventions are then <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium">built</strong> to repair that mismatch. And when a fixed intervention cannot cover every context, the system may need to <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium">adapt</strong> to the person using it. Each stage produces measurement, artifacts, and open questions that feed the next — this is conceptual program framing, not an empirical claim.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. Current focus -->
      <section id="focus" class="mb-12">
        <div class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-secondary)] bg-[var(--color-secondary-subtle)]/40 rounded-r-lg px-5 py-4">
          <p class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] font-semibold text-[var(--color-secondary-dim)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Current focus</p>
          <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-2">
            CheckMyCoach human validation toward the combined Precision Illusion + CheckMyCoach paper. No completed human-participant findings are claimed.
          </p>
          <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/checkmycoach/" class="link-arrow">CheckMyCoach project →</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Methods / infrastructure (secondary) -->
      <section id="methods">
        <span class="section-kicker mb-2">Methods &amp; infrastructure</span>
        <h2 class="mt-1 mb-3">Reusable assets</h2>
        <div class="related-list">
          <div class="related-item">
            <span class="rel-role">Measurement &amp; taxonomy</span>
            <span class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)]">Precision Illusion taxonomy · FitCalib-Bench audit</span>
          </div>
          <div class="related-item">
            <span class="rel-role">Experimental infrastructure</span>
            <span class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)]">InteractionKit v1.0.0 — typed experiment infrastructure</span>
          </div>
          <div class="related-item">
            <span class="rel-role">Provenance-aware knowledge</span>
            <span class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)]">Knowledge Compiler — corpus artifact, no validity claim</span>
          </div>
          <div class="related-item">
            <span class="rel-role">Evaluation tooling</span>
            <span class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)]">CheckMyCoach offline pipeline · interactive demo</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
